What is retained from the original
----------------------------------
  * the PS/2 (PlayStation 2) wire protocol implementation, including the
    bit-banging order, the ACK slot handling and the configuration command set
    (enter_config, set_mode, set_bytes_large, exit_config, enable_rumble,
    type_read);
  * the button, analog-stick and pressure constants (PSB_*, PSS_*, PSAB_*);
  * the public class name `PS2X`, all public method names and the header name
    `PS2X_lib.h`, so that existing sketches are source compatible;
  * the overall structure of the driver (config → read → getters).

Statement of changes (GPLv3 § 5 a)
----------------------------------
  Modified in 2026 by LROB.RU — https://lrob.ru
  (GitHub: https://github.com/delsolru)

  * Replaced the AVR-only I/O layer (avr/io.h, SREG/cli(), portOutputRegister,
    digitalPinToBitMask) with a portable GPIO abstraction: direct AVR port
    registers, direct ESP32 GPIO registers (GPIO_OUT_W1TS / GPIO_IN) and a
    digitalWrite/digitalRead fallback for other cores.
  * Added cycle-counter based microsecond delays on ESP32 (esp_cpu_get_ccount)
    so the bus timing no longer depends on delayMicroseconds() or on the CPU
    frequency.
  * Added the diagnostics API: lastError(), ok()/connected(), failedReads(),
    lastOkAge(), frameMicros(), errorText(), typeText(), debugPrint(), rawPacket().
  * Added hot-plug recovery, pin validation (PS2X_ERR_BAD_PIN), runtime tunable
    bit timing (setTiming()) and read-rate control (setReadDelay()).
  * read_gamepad() now returns bool instead of void (source compatible).
  * Rewrote the documentation (README.md, README.ru.md, CHANGELOG*.md, this
    NOTICE), added examples, packaging metadata (library.properties,
    library.json) and CI.

None of the original copyright notices were removed. The complete text of the
licence is in LICENSE. The full list of changes is in CHANGELOG.md /
CHANGELOG.ru.md and, commit by commit, in this repository's git history — the
first commit is the pristine upstream code this edition was derived from.

